> For an unflagged query, `direct_with_plan` has much lower estimated cost/latency, so it wins. Its hidden `RESEARCH_PLAN` footer is currently only parsed and returned—it does **not** trigger a second search execution.
> 
> Make “research required” a hard eligibility constraint before utility scoring, rather than trying to overpower the cost term with cue bonuses.
